.TH SISTA-FIELD 3 "" "Sista" "Library Functions Manual"
.SH NAME
sista-field \- fields, coordinates, borders, and pawns
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sista/field.hpp>
.B #include <sista/pawn.hpp>
.B #include <sista/border.hpp>
.B #include <sista/coordinates.hpp>
.PP
.B c++ program.cpp \-lSista
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Field
models a rectangular terminal area containing pawns.
A
.B Pawn
has a character, coordinates, and ANSI settings.
A
.B Border
describes the character and appearance used around a printed field.
.PP
Pawns are normally owned through
.B std::shared_ptr<Pawn>.
Adding a pawn associates it with the field; movement and removal operations
must use a pawn that belongs to the relevant field.
.PP
.B SwappableField
extends
.B Field
with deferred movement.
Call
.B addPawnToSwap()
for each intended movement and then
.B applySwaps()
to apply the batch.
This is useful when several pawns move during the same frame.
.SH COORDINATES
.B Coordinates
stores a row and column as y and x.
Field dimensions and bounds should be checked before movement.
The
.B Effect::PACMAN
movement effect wraps out-of-bounds coordinates, while
.B Effect::MATRIX
turns horizontal overflow into movement between adjacent rows.
Matrix movement fails if the resulting row is outside the field.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
#include <memory>
#include <sista/sista.hpp>

int main()
{
    sista::Field field(20, 8);
    auto pawn = std::make_shared<sista::Pawn>(
        '@', sista::Coordinates(2, 3), sista::ANSISettings());

    field.addPawn(pawn);
    field.print('#');
}
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR sista (3),
.BR sista-ansi (3)
